          "distinct": false,
          "id": "50f7e2d56f99fbdb8a61bb3b0c4b1fa3c394ca68",
          "message": "bench(reason): same-box materialization comparison — sparq OWL-RL/RDFS closure vs Jena / VLog / Nemo on LUBM (sq-hmd7l.7) [FABLE-5] (#1799)\n\n🤖 SPARQ agent. Adds scripts/bench/materialize-same-box.sh (envelope mirrors\nshacl-same-box.sh) comparing sparq `reason` (OWL-RL / RDFS) closure vs Apache\nJena rule reasoners vs VLog vs Nemo over the SAME LUBM (ABox+TBox) N-Triples at\nuniv=1/10 locally. Fills the D6 (materialization) gap row, previously NOT-MEASURED.\n\n- Oracle = closure-size cross-check; pinned univ=1 (owl=150589, rdfs=126732)\n  asserted by the harness (acceptance: ONLY=sparq LUBM_UNIVS=1 exits 0).\n- Profile/rule-set fidelity recorded PER COLUMN, never absorbed: sparq owl =\n  full W3C OWL 2 RL/RDF; Jena OWL_MICRO/OWL_MINI/RDFS are OWL-SUBSET reasoners +\n  add axiomatic triples + de-dup on load (closure size differs by construction);\n  VLog/Nemo are general Datalog needing a separately-validated encoding.\n- Jena driver: scripts/bench-adapters/jena_reason_adapter.java (in-process\n  InfModel materialize best-of-N). VLog/Nemo adapters emit honest NOT-RUN-LOCALLY\n  with the exact install/encoding blocker (never a fabricated number).\n- bench/lubm/gen.sh READ-ONLY; run.sh untouched. All work-box numbers are\n  NON-canonical (PR body only); research/gap-materialize-2026-07.md is the\n  first-read record and carries NO hard-coded perf numbers.\n\nFollow-ups beaded: sq-hmd7l.30 (validated VLog encoding), sq-hmd7l.31 (validated\nNemo encoding), sq-hmd7l.32 (canonical univ>=100 EC2 run).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <jesse@jeswr.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-09T22:12:14Z",
          "tree_id": "2d4abc461c7ed0736788544f7cfe54a7be370023",
